    {
      "id": 21,
      "type": "text",
      "title": "How to interpret the simulation",
      "gridPos": {"x": 0, "y": 20, "w": 24, "h": 5},
      "options": {"mode": "markdown", "content": "**This is the live-equivalent paper account.** It uses current public Polymarket books, walks executable liquidity, simulates fills, charges protocol fees and slippage, marks open positions to executable bids, and applies the same sizing and drawdown controls. A PnL of zero is meaningful only when **Simulator State = RUNNING** and **Data Staleness** is low; otherwise zero must not be interpreted as trading performance. Maker and multi-leg sleeves remain separate below and are not added to the main account, avoiding double-counting capital. No authenticated real-money order submission is enabled."}
